The upstream exponential approximation identifies its algorithm as derived
from the public-domain fdlibm e_exp.c implementation.

The adaptation replaces architecture-specific randomness access with the
portable expansion module, uses explicit little-endian loads, checked sizing
and output conversion, and adds numerical domain checks. It is experimental.

The experimental short-challenge reference in portable/challenge.rs and its
roots.rs table are adapted from poly.c at the same labrados commit, under the
same IBM copyright and Apache-2.0 license. The Rust adaptation replaces SIMD
polynomial storage with canonical portable ring values and retains the scalar
FFT constants and sampling schedule for reference compatibility testing.
